Be extremely concise. Never repeat generated code at the end of a reply. Do not add "key code references" dumps.

## Product
CoDev is a **web-hosted** collaborative workspace (trycodev.com), not a desktop app.

## Commands
Run from the repository root with **pnpm**. Node 24+.
`pnpm install` · `pnpm dev` · `pnpm format:check` · `pnpm lint` · `pnpm typecheck` · `pnpm test` · `pnpm build` · `pnpm test:e2e` · `pnpm rust:check` · `pnpm orca:web`

Do not add Dockerfiles or Docker Compose. Use Apple `container` if local containers are needed.

## Monorepo
- Check sibling files in the same package before inventing a pattern.
- Prefer `packages/contracts`, Zod, and Drizzle schema over ad hoc types.
- `packages/ide` is excluded from the root workspace. Never include it in root recursive pnpm/Prettier. Use its own tooling.

## Safety
- Credentials stay server-only. Never put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Private GitHub credentials must not appear in URLs, argv, logs, browser pairing data, or persisted remotes.
- Keep Vercel (web) vs AWS (Firecracker/Orca) separate.
- Sandbox vs IDE filesystems are isolated. Use sandbox API vs `/ide` routes correctly.

## Git / Vercel
Keep diffs scoped. Do not commit or push unless asked. Each branch push starts a Vercel preview; `main` is production. One coherent commit per change. Add or update tests when behavior changes.
